\"\",\"url\":\"\",\"relevance\":\"\"}]\n}\nTone: concise, authoritative, and practical. Use complete sentences.\nObservations: 4–6 items, each with a headline and 2–4 sentences of detail.\nCitations: 3–5 items; provide APA style in \"apa\" and a 1–2 sentence relevance note.\nArticle:\n{\"id\":\"smart-manufacturing-workforce-2024\",\"title\":\"The Workforce for Smart Manufacturing: Adapting Skills and Roles in the Era of AI-Driven Automation\",\"brief\":\"This article analyzes how AI and automation are remaking the factory workforce\\u2014outlining crucial upskilling paths, new job roles, and change management strategies for manufacturers facing an unprecedented transformation.\",\"keywords\":[\"manufacturing workforce\",\"AI upskilling\",\"automation jobs\",\"industrial digitalization\",\"change management\",\"workforce transformation\"],\"recommended_word_count\":\"1500-2500\",\"topic_coverage_level\":\"Important and Not Covered\"}\nCitations:\n[{\"title\":\"59 AI Job Statistics: Future of U.S. Jobs | National University\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.nu.edu\\/blog\\/ai-job-statistics\\/\",\"source\":\"www.nu.edu\",\"snippet\":\"Discover how artificial intelligence is transforming the U.S. job market with 59 key AI job statistics covering automation risks and more.\"},{\"title\":\"Assessing the Real Impact of Automation on Jobs | Stanford HAI\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/hai.stanford.edu\\/news\\/assessing-the-real-impact-of-automation-on-jobs\",\"source\":\"hai.stanford.edu\",\"snippet\":\"MIT economist David Autor argues that focusing on exposure alone misses the nuances of how experts and nonexperts experience task shifts.\"},{\"title\":\"2025 Smart manufacturing survey | Deloitte Insights\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.deloitte.com\\/us\\/en\\/insights\\/industry\\/manufacturing\\/2025-smart-manufacturing-survey.html\",\"source\":\"www.deloitte.com\",\"snippet\":\"This study shows how smart factories boost agility, attract talent and increase productivity. Learn the challenges, technologies and practices of industry 4.0.\"},{\"title\":\"Automation and the workforce of the future | McKinsey\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.mckinsey.com\\/featured-insights\\/future-of-work\\/skill-shift-automation-and-the-future-of-the-workforce\",\"source\":\"www.mckinsey.com\",\"snippet\":\"\"},{\"title\":\"AI: Work partnerships between people, agents, and robots | McKinsey\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.mckinsey.com\\/mgi\\/our-research\\/agents-robots-and-us-skill-partnerships-in-the-age-of-ai\",\"source\":\"www.mckinsey.com\",\"snippet\":\"\"}]','{\"id\":\"chatcmpl-D3mVAU0fExezPCtVYOQwwlvgXdgqy\",\"object\":\"chat.completion\",\"created\":1769793796,\"model\":\"gpt-5.2-2025-12-11\",\"choices\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"{\\n  \\\"framework\\\": {\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Editorial Framework: The Workforce for Smart Manufacturing in the Era of AI-Driven Automation\\\",\\n    \\\"overview\\\": \\\"This framework structures an article on how AI, advanced automation, and data-centric operations are reshaping manufacturing work. It prioritizes actionable guidance for leaders who must redesign roles, build new skill pathways, and manage workforce change while sustaining productivity and safety.\\\",\\n    \\\"context\\\": \\\"Smart manufacturing initiatives are moving from experimentation to value realization, but adoption increases pressure on talent acquisition, cybersecurity, and change management. Research shows automation typically reallocates tasks rather than simply eliminating jobs, shifting demand toward more abstract, digital, and cross-functional capabilities. Manufacturers need a workforce strategy that links technology deployment to task redesign, capability building, and measurable outcomes.\\\",\\n    \\\"application\\\": {\\n      \\\"intended_reader\\\": \\\"Manufacturing executives, plant managers, operations leaders, and HR\\/L&D partners responsible for Industry 4.0 transformation.\\\",\\n      \\\"use_case\\\": \\\"Use this plan to outline a 1,500\\u20132,500 word article that explains workforce impacts, defines emerging roles, and provides a practical upskilling and change-management playbook.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"observations\\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\\"headline\\\": \\\"Automation changes task composition more than headcount outcomes.\\\",\\n        \\\"detail\\\": \\\"Automation exposure alone is a poor predictor of job loss because roles evolve based on which tasks are removed versus added. Evidence suggests routine tasks are disproportionately eliminated while more abstract tasks are added, raising the importance of judgment, problem-solving, and higher-value support work. Editorially, frame workforce impact as a task redesign challenge, not just a staffing debate.\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"headline\\\": \\\"Smart factory value is arriving, but workforce and transformation maturity lag.\\\",\\n        \\\"detail\\\": \\\"As smart manufacturing scales, organizations report measurable improvements in output, productivity, and capacity, which increases executive willingness to invest. At the same time, manufacturers often rate human capital maturity lower than operational and technology domains, indicating a predictable bottleneck. The article should emphasize sequencing: build adoption plans that include workforce readiness as a first-order workstream.\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"headline\\\": \\\"Skill demand is shifting toward digital fluency, higher cognitive work, and human collaboration.\\\",\\n        \\\"detail\\\": \\\"Long-run modeling indicates rising demand for advanced and basic digital skills alongside social and emotional skills, while physical\\/manual and basic cognitive skills decline in relative importance. AI further accelerates a \\u201cpartnership\\u201d model where humans coordinate, validate, and improve machine-driven workflows. For manufacturers, this implies broader baseline digital capability across frontline roles, not only specialists.\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"headline\\\": \\\"New roles emerge at the intersection of OT, IT, data, and safety.\\\",\\n        \\\"detail\\\": \\\"AI-driven operations increase demand for hybrid talent such as automation technicians with data skills, industrial data engineers, OT cybersecurity specialists, and digital production leaders. These roles typically require cross-functional literacy and clear accountability for model performance, process control, and risk. The article should include a role taxonomy and a transition map from legacy roles into hybrid profiles.\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"headline\\\": \\\"Change management is a capability, not a communication plan.\\\",\\n        \\\"detail\\\": \\\"Smart manufacturing transformations create operational risk if adoption outpaces training, governance, and cultural alignment. Research on smart manufacturing highlights the need for dedicated internal teams to manage change and organizational transformation, plus stronger cybersecurity controls. Editorial guidance should convert this into concrete practices: supervisor enablement, frontline engagement loops, and metrics tied to adoption and quality outcomes.\\\"\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \\\"key_themes\\\": [\\n      \\\"Task redesign and human-machine collaboration\\\",\\n      \\\"Frontline digital fluency and AI-enabled work\\\",\\n      \\\"Hybrid roles bridging OT\\/IT\\/data\\\",\\n      \\\"Upskilling pathways and credentialing\\\",\\n      \\\"Change management and transformation governance\\\",\\n      \\\"Operational risk, cybersecurity, and safety in smart factories\\\"\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  \\\"citations\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"apa\\\": \\\"Garrison, K. G. (2025, June 9). Assessing the real impact of automation on jobs. Stanford Institute for Human-Centered Artificial Intelligence (HAI).\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/hai.stanford.edu\\/news\\/assessing-the-real-impact-of-automation-on-jobs\\\",\\n      \\\"relevance\\\": \\\"Provides a nuanced task-based view of automation impacts, including evidence that routine tasks are disproportionately removed and abstract tasks added. Useful for arguing that workforce planning should focus on task shifts and skill barriers, not simplistic job-loss projections.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"apa\\\": \\\"Gaus, T., & Schlotterbeck, M. (2025, May 1). 2025 smart manufacturing and operations survey: Navigating challenges to implementation. Deloitte Insights.\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.deloitte.com\\/us\\/en\\/insights\\/industry\\/manufacturing\\/2025-smart-manufacturing-survey.html\\\",\\n      \\\"relevance\\\": \\\"Documents that smart manufacturing is increasingly viewed as a competitiveness driver and reports operational, productivity, and capacity improvements. Also highlights implementation obstacles and the need for workforce upskilling and dedicated change teams, directly supporting the article\\u2019s action agenda.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"apa\\\": \\\"Bughin, J., Hazan, E., Lund, S., Dahlstr\\u00f6m, P., Wiesinger, A., & Subramaniam, A. (2018, May 23). Skill shift: Automation and the future of the workforce. McKinsey Global Institute.\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.mckinsey.com\\/featured-insights\\/future-of-work\\/skill-shift-automation-and-the-future-of-the-workforce\\\",\\n      \\\"relevance\\\": \\\"Quantifies how automation shifts demand toward technological, social\\/emotional, and higher cognitive skills through 2030. Supports editorial recommendations on upskilling priorities for manufacturing operations and leadership.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"apa\\\": \\\"Yee, L., Madgavkar, A., Smit, S., Krivkovich, A., Chui, M., Ram\\u00edrez, M. J., & Castresana, D. (2025, November 25). Agents, robots, and us: Skill partnerships in the age of AI. McKinsey Global Institute.\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.mckinsey.com\\/mgi\\/our-research\\/agents-robots-and-us-skill-partnerships-in-the-age-of-ai\\\",\\n      \\\"relevance\\\": \\\"Introduces a \\u201cpeople, agents, and robots\\u201d partnership model and highlights rapid growth in employer demand for AI fluency. Useful for positioning smart manufacturing roles around workflow redesign, human oversight, and AI governance rather than isolated automation use cases.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\",\"refusal\":null,\"annotations\":[]},\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}],\"usage\":{\"prompt_tokens\":11247,\"completion_tokens\":1380,\"total_tokens\":12627,\"prompt_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":0,\"audio_tokens\":0},\"completion_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":0,\"audio_tokens\":0,\"accepted_prediction_tokens\":0,\"rejected_prediction_tokens\":0}},\"service_tier\":\"default\",\"system_fingerprint\":null}',NULL,NULL,'1',11247,1380,420210,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1,'planner-fw-d12abca8-89ba416a','2026-01-30 17:23:00','2026-01-30 17:23:40'),('0ee56b09-8fe9-47d5-ad96-d692aae909a1','a38c0b3c-9f4b-4b47-a1bc-e03e2380cd57',NULL,'gpt-5.2','failed','Act as an Editorial Planning Assistant. Create a structured framework that is ready for human consumption.\nReturn ONLY valid JSON.\nSchema:\n{\n\"framework\":{\n  \"title\":\"\",\n  \"overview\":\"\",\n  \"context\":\"\",\n  \"application\":{\"intended_reader\":\"\",\"use_case\":\"\"},\n  \"observations\":[{\"headline\":\"\",\"detail\":\"\"}],\n  \"key_themes\":[\"\"]\n},\n\"citations\":[{\"apa\":\"\",\"url\":\"\",\"relevance\":\"\"}]\n}\nTone: concise, authoritative, and practical. Use complete sentences.\nObservations: 4–6 items, each with a headline and 2–4 sentences of detail.\nCitations: 3–5 items; provide APA style in \"apa\" and a 1–2 sentence relevance note.\nArticle:\n{\n    \"id\": \"ai-automation-smart-manufacturing-trends-2024\",\n    \"title\": \"AI-Driven Automation in Manufacturing: How Smart Factories Will Transform 2024\\u2019s Industrial Landscape\",\n    \"brief\": \"Explore how manufacturers are levera