eas: Field Service Management, Spare Parts Management, B2B Manufacturing E-Commerce, B2B Manufacturing Pricing, Servitization, Aftermarket Strategy.\nFor e-commerce & pricing, focus exclusively on B2B manufacturing.\nReturn ONLY valid JSON. Do not include commentary.\nSchema: {\n\"executive_summary\":\"\",\n\"trends\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"insight\":\"\",\"implications_for_articles\":[\"\"],\"sources\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"url\":\"\",\"source\":\"\",\"type\":\"\",\"date\":\"\",\"snippet\":\"\"}]}],\n\"trend_summary\":[{\"trend\":\"\",\"repeated_in_research\":\"yes|no|mixed\"}],\n\"sources\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"url\":\"\",\"source\":\"\",\"type\":\"\",\"date\":\"\",\"snippet\":\"\"}],\n\"next_step_question\":\"Proceed to Phase 2?\"\n}\nGather 16 distinct sources from the first two pages of results. No duplicate domains. Mix reports, white papers, news, expert blogs, academic papers.\nFocus on 2023-2026 sources. No invented metadata.','{\"id\":\"chatcmpl-D2bQZDhY4trTOooTOnqF7I9jHfFNc\",\"object\":\"chat.completion\",\"created\":1769512899,\"model\":\"gpt-4-0613\",\"choices\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":null,\"tool_calls\":[{\"id\":\"call_tbcGJDBcomyk87MEmLwYK45L\",\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"web_search\",\"arguments\":\"{\\n  \\\"query\\\": \\\"B2B Manufacturing Pricing trends 2023-2026\\\",\\n  \\\"top_k\\\": 8\\n}\"}}],\"refusal\":null,\"annotations\":[]},\"logprobs\":null,\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"}],\"usage\":{\"prompt_tokens\":2300,\"completion_tokens\":34,\"total_tokens\":2334,\"prompt_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":0,\"audio_tokens\":0},\"completion_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":0,\"audio_tokens\":0,\"accepted_prediction_tokens\":0,\"rejected_prediction_tokens\":0}},\"service_tier\":\"default\",\"system_fingerprint\":null}',NULL,NULL,'1',2300,34,71040,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1,'planner-phase1-5d7b0607-2f25-441d-a97b-e022e02a7f2e-1769512892','2026-01-27 11:21:33','2026-01-27 11:21:41'),('20ab07a5-8391-43da-8c19-ebc29efcb812','a38c0b3c-9f4b-4b47-a1bc-e03e2380cd57',NULL,'gpt-4.1','completed','You are the Author Agent. Write a draft article based on the provided framework.\nReturn ONLY valid JSON.\nSchema: {\"title\":\"\",\"draft\":\"\",\"key_points\":[\"\"],\"citations\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"url\":\"\",\"quote\":\"\"}]}\nArticle headline: AI-Driven Automation in Manufacturing: How Smart Factories Will Transform 2024’s Industrial Landscape\nSynopsis: Explore how manufacturers are leveraging AI, robotics, and digital twins to drive efficiency, quality, and operational resilience. This article provides a data-backed look at adoption trends, real-world use cases, and the near-future of smart manufacturing in a post-pandemic economy.\nKeywords: AI-driven automation, smart manufacturing, digital twins, industrial robots, factory efficiency, manufacturing transformation\nFramework:\n{\"title\":\"Editorial Framework: AI-Driven Automation in Manufacturing (Smart Factories) \\u2014 2024 Playbook\",\"overview\":\"This framework structures a 1,500\\u20132,500 word article explaining how AI, robotics, and digital twins are moving smart factories from pilots to measurable operational impact. It emphasizes what is changing in 2024: faster scaling, workflow redesign, and tighter governance, cybersecurity, and workforce enablement. The goal is to connect technology choices to concrete plant-floor outcomes (throughput, quality, uptime, and resilience).\",\"context\":\"Manufacturers are accelerating smart manufacturing programs as supply volatility and margin pressure reward higher productivity, agility, and operational transparency. Recent surveys show broad conviction that smart manufacturing will drive competitiveness, but many initiatives still face common barriers: talent gaps, complex transformations, and operational risk. Editorially, the opportunity is to translate the \\u201csmart factory\\u201d concept into an actionable roadmap with examples and metrics readers can use to benchmark progress.\",\"application\":{\"intended_reader\":\"Manufacturing executives, plant leaders, operations\\/OT leaders, and digital transformation program owners.\",\"use_case\":\"Use this framework to outline a practical, evidence-led article that prioritizes high-value use cases (quality, throughput, maintenance, and planning), clarifies enabling capabilities (data foundation, digital twins, robotics, and AI), and provides implementation guardrails (cybersecurity, governance, and workforce upskilling).\"},\"observations\":[{\"headline\":\"Smart manufacturing is shifting from promise to value realization.\",\"detail\":\"Large-scale survey evidence indicates manufacturers increasingly view smart manufacturing as a competitiveness driver over the near term. Reported impacts cluster around output, productivity, and capacity gains rather than abstract \\u201cdigital transformation\\u201d narratives. The article should foreground specific operational KPIs and show how they are achieved (instrumentation, analytics, and process changes), not just the technologies involved.\"},{\"headline\":\"Scaling is still the hard part; workflow redesign is a differentiator.\",\"detail\":\"Across industries, many organizations remain stuck in experimentation or piloting, even as AI use becomes common. The strongest results correlate with redesigning workflows and embedding AI into day-to-day decision loops, not simply deploying models. Position 2024 as the year manufacturers move from isolated pilots (e.g., one line) to repeatable patterns (multi-site playbooks).\"},{\"headline\":\"Digital twins and AI converge as the operating model for the modern plant.\",\"detail\":\"Digital twins are most compelling when paired with AI for prediction, optimization, and closed-loop control\\u2014especially in bottleneck management, quality, and asset performance. The narrative should explain how twins connect engineering, operations, and maintenance via a common data layer. Include guidance on where to start (one asset\\/line, then expand) and what \\u201cdone\\u201d looks like (validated models, governed data, and measurable KPI lift).\"},{\"headline\":\"Robotics adoption is being reshaped by AI, autonomy, and orchestration.\",\"detail\":\"Robots are increasingly integrated into broader automation platforms where AI coordinates tasks, exceptions, and real-time work allocation. This changes vendor decisions and architecture: manufacturers must plan for interoperability, orchestration, and process intelligence rather than single-point automations. Emphasize selection criteria that reduce integration risk (open interfaces, OT compatibility, and lifecycle support).\"},{\"headline\":\"Cybersecurity, governance, and skills are now first-order constraints.\",\"detail\":\"As plants connect more assets and deploy more autonomous capabilities, operational risk expands and requires stronger controls, oversight models, and cyber investment. Multiple reports highlight that governance maturity can lag technology adoption, especially for more autonomous systems. The article should provide a practical checklist: governance roles, model monitoring, OT security controls, and workforce upskilling plans.\"}],\"key_themes\":[\"From pilots to scale: repeatable use-case factories and multi-site rollout patterns.\",\"Digital twins + AI for predictive and prescriptive operations.\",\"Robotics and automation orchestration as a platform strategy.\",\"Operational KPIs: throughput, quality, OEE, capacity unlock, and downtime reduction.\",\"Risk management: cybersecurity, governance, and safe autonomy.\",\"Workforce enablement: upskilling, human-in-the-loop operations, and change management.\"]}\nCitations:\n[{\"apa\":\"Gaus, T., & Schlotterbeck, M. (2025, May 1). 2025 Smart Manufacturing and Operations Survey: Navigating challenges to implementation. Deloitte Insights.\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.deloitte.com\\/us\\/en\\/insights\\/industry\\/manufacturing\\/2025-smart-manufacturing-survey.html\",\"relevance\":\"Provides manufacturing-specific survey data on perceived competitiveness drivers and reported improvements (e.g., output, productivity, and capacity), plus common implementation challenges such as talent and operational risk.\"},{\"apa\":\"Singla, A., Sukharevsky, A., Hall, B., Yee, L., & Chui, M. (2025, November 5). The state of AI in 2025: Agents, innovation, and transformation. McKinsey & Company.\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.mckinsey.com\\/capabilities\\/quantumblack\\/our-insights\\/the-state-of-ai\",\"relevance\":\"Documents that AI use is widespread but scaling remains limited, and highlights workflow redesign as a key success factor. Useful to frame why manufacturers must move beyond pilots to capture enterprise-level value.\"},{\"apa\":\"Deloitte. (2026). The State of AI in the Enterprise: Deloitte\\u2019s 2026 AI report tracking adoption and impact. Deloitte AI Institute.\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.deloitte.com\\/us\\/en\\/what-we-do\\/capabilities\\/applied-artificial-intelligence\\/content\\/state-of-ai-in-the-enterprise.html\",\"relevance\":\"Adds enterprise AI adoption context, including access expansion, governance gaps for agentic systems, and the primacy of AI fluency\\/skills development\\u2014directly supporting the article\\u2019s governance and workforce sections.\"},{\"apa\":\"Gartner. (n.d.). Smart factory trends for manufacturing industries. Gartner.\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.gartner.com\\/en\\/supply-chain\\/trends\\/smart-factory-trends\",\"relevance\":\"Defines smart factory operations as a strategic trend and frames practical questions leaders ask: measuring value, core technologies used, lessons learned, and success factors. Useful for structuring the article into decision-oriented sections.\"},{\"apa\":\"Le Clair, C., & Schaffrik, B. (2024, February 23). AI is reshaping automation markets: A guide to process tool evolution. Forrester.\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.forrester.com\\/report\\/ai-is-reshaping-automation-markets\\/RES180584\",\"relevance\":\"Supports the platformization theme: consolidation of automation tool markets and a shift toward \\u201cautomation fabric\\u201d concepts. This helps explain why orchestration and integrated process intelligence matter for manufacturing automation strategies.\"}]','{\"id\":\"chatcmpl-D3Vk9bUVUdlRn7RguxMMZ6rJjpt8N\",\"object\":\"chat.completion\",\"created\":1769729377,\"model\":\"gpt-4.1-2025-04-14\",\"choices\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"{\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"AI-Driven Automation in Manufacturing: How Smart Factories Will Transform 2024\\u2019s Industrial Landscape\\\",\\n  \\\"draft\\\": \\\"In 2024, the manufacturing sector stands at a pivotal moment: AI-driven automation is moving from isolated pilots to scaled, measurable impact across the industrial landscape. Manufacturers are increasingly adopting smart factory technologies\\u2014including artificial intelligence (AI), robotics, and digital twins\\u2014not just as buzzwords, but as key drivers of competitiveness, resilience, and sustainable growth.\\\\n\\\\n## From Promise to Value Realization: The Data-Backed Imperative\\\\nRecent survey data underscores the urgency and rewards of embracing smart manufacturing. According to Deloitte\\u2019s 2025 Smart Manufacturing and Operations Survey, a significant majority of manufacturing executives report that smart factory initiatives have delivered improvements in output, productivity, and capacity\\u2014not merely theoretical \\u201cdigital transformation.\\u201d As manufacturers contend with supply volatility and mounting margin pressures, 2024 marks an inflection point: those investing in actionable AI and automation are seeing higher throughput, better quality, and increased operational transparency [1].\\\\n\\\\n## Beyond Pilots: Scaling Requires Workflow Redesign\\\\nWhile AI is now widely deployed on the plant floor, the leap from isolated experimentation to enterprise-wide value remains challenging. McKinsey\\u2019s 2025 State of AI research finds that organizations capturing the greatest performance gains do so by embedding AI into everyday workflows, redesigning processes\\u2014not simply deploying point solutions [2]. In 2024, leading manufacturers are codifying lessons from successful pilots into multi-site playbooks, focusing on high-value use cases like predictive maintenance, automated quality inspection, and throughput optimization.\\\\n\\\\n## Digital Twins Meet AI: The Next Operating Model\\\\nDigital twins\\u2014the virtual replicas of physical assets and processes\\u2014are reaching new maturity as they converge with AI. When connected to real-time data streams and predictive analytics, digital twins become engines for operational improvement: they enable scenario modeling, predictive maintenance, and closed-loop quality management. The most effective digital twin programs begin with a targeted asset or line, validate data flows and models, then expand incrementally, creating a governed foundation for plant-wide transformation [3].\\\\n\\\\n## Robotics and the Shift to Automation Platforms\\\\nTraditional, single-task robot deployments are giving way to highly orchestrated automation platforms. AI now coordinates robots, sensors, and interfaces\\u2014allocating work, managing exceptions, and optimizing tasks in real time. This platformization, as identified by Forrester, requires manufacturers to rethink vendor selection and integration: open APIs, interoperability, and lifecycle support are essential criteria. The shift is clear\\u2014future-ready manufacturers invest not in standalone robots, but in automation ecosystems that enhance flexibility, traceability, and resilience [5].\\\\n\\\\n## Managing Risks: Cybersecurity, Governance, and Workforce Upskilling\\\\nAs smart factories grow more connected and autonomous, operational risks multiply. Cybersecurity and governance are no longer afterthoughts; they are strategic imperatives. Deloitte\\u2019s AI in the Enterprise report emphasizes the lag in governance maturity, particularly as manufacturers introduce more autonomous and agentic systems. Leaders must implement robust OT security controls, establish clear governance roles, and invest in continuous monitoring of AI models. Equally important is workforce enablement: upskilling workers to collaborate with AI, manage exceptions, and drive change on the factory floor is as critical as any technology investment [3].\\\\n\\\\n## Practical Roadmap for 2024\\u2019s Smart Factory Transformation\\\\nManufacturers ready to scale should prioritize:\\\\n- Starting with high-value, repeatable use cases (quality, throughput, predictive maintenance)\\\\n- Building a trusted data foundation for AI and digital twins\\\\n- Selecting automation platforms with open integration and orchestration capabilities\\\\n- Implementing strong cybersecurity and governance frameworks\\\\n- Investing in workforce upskilling and change management programs\\\\nThis concerted, practical approach moves smart manufacturing from vision to measurable competitive advantage. In 2024 and beyond, the factories that thrive will be those that turn AI-driven automation into both operational excellence and a resilient, future-ready business model.\\\",\\n  \\\"key_points\\\": [\\n    \\\"Manufacturers are scaling smart factory initiatives from pilots to enterprise-level deployment, driven by tangible improvements in productivity and competitiveness.\\\",\\n    \\\"Success hinges on workflow redesign and embedding AI into daily operations\\u2014not just deploying point automation or isolated AI models.\\\",\\n    \\\"Digital twins, paired with AI, are becoming the operating backbone for predictive maintenance, performance optimization, and process integration.\\\",\\n    \\\"Robotics strategy is shifting toward automation platforms and orchestration, requiring interoperability and process intelligence over single-task automation.\\\",\\n    \\\"Cybersecurity, governance, and workforce upskilling are now first-order priorities as factories become more autonomous and interconnected.\\\",\\n    \\\"A practical, phased roadmap focusing on high-value use cases, data readiness, and risk management is essential for scaling smart manufacturing in 2024.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"citations\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"2025 Smart Manufacturing and Operations Survey: Navigating challenges to implementation\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.deloitte.com\\/us\\/en\\/insights\\/industry\\/manufacturing\\/2025-smart-manufacturing-survey.html\\\",\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Smart factory initiatives have delivered measurable improvements in output, productivity, and capacity according to a majority of surveyed manufacturing executives.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"The state of AI in 2025: Agents, innovation, and transformation\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.mckinsey.com\\/capabilities\\/quantumblack\\/our-insights\\/the-state-of-ai\\\",\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"AI use is widespread but scaling remains limited; workflow redesign is a key factor in achieving enterprise-level value.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"The State of AI in the Enterprise: Deloitte\\u2019s 2026 AI report tracking adoption and impact\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.deloitte.com\\/us\\/en\\/what-we-do\\/capabilities\\/applied-artificial-intelligence\\/content\\/state-of-ai-in-the-enterprise.html\\\",\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Governance maturity can lag technology adoption, especially for more autonomous systems; workforce enablement is critical for successful AI integration.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Smart factory trends for manufacturing industries\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.gartner.com\\/en\\/supply-chain\\/trends\\/smart-factory-trends\\\",\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Defines smart factory operations as a strategic trend and highlights key decision areas: value measurement, technology selection, and lessons learned.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"AI is reshaping automation markets: A guide to process tool evolution\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.forrester.com\\/report\\/ai-is-reshaping-automation-markets\\/RES180584\\\",\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Manufacturers should move toward automation platform strategies, prioritizing interoperability, orchestration, and integrated process intelligence.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\",\"refusal\":null,\"annotations\":[]},\"logprobs\":null,\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}],\"usage\":{\"prompt_tokens\":1846,\"completion_tokens\":1388,\"total_tokens\":3234,\"prompt_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":0,\"audio_tokens\":0},\"completion_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":0,\"audio_tokens\":0,\"accepted_prediction_tokens\":0,\"rejected_prediction_tokens\":0}},\"service_tier\":\"default\",\"system_fingerprint\":\"fp_6deacce395\"}',NULL,NULL,'1',1846,1388,60100,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1,'planner-author-d12abca8-83b584c8-1769729375','2026-01-29 23:29:36','2026-01-29 23:30:01'),('21f9b9d6-eef2-4135-a22b-e4c383556fcb','a38c0b3c-9f4b-4b47-a1bc-e03e2380cd57',NULL,'gpt-4.1','completed','You are the Author Agent. Write a draft article based on the provided framework.\nReturn ONLY valid JSON.\nSchema: {\"title\":\"\",\"draft\":\"\",\"key_points\":[\"\"],\"citations\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"url\":\"\",\"quote\":\"\"}]}\nArticle headline: AI-Driven Automation in Manufacturing: How Smart Factories Will Transform 2024’s Industrial Landscape\nSynopsis: Explore how manufacturers are leveraging AI, robotics, and digital twins to drive efficiency, quality, and operational resilience. This article provides a data-backed look at adoption trends, real-world use cases, and the near-future of smart manufacturing in a post-pandemic economy.\nKeywords: AI-driven automation, smart manufacturing, digital twins, industrial robots, factory e