tonomous capabilities, operational risk expands and requires stronger controls, oversight models, and cyber investment. Multiple reports highlight that governance maturity can lag technology adoption, especially for more autonomous systems. The article should provide a practical checklist: governance roles, model monitoring, OT security controls, and workforce upskilling plans.\"}],\"key_themes\":[\"From pilots to scale: repeatable use-case factories and multi-site rollout patterns.\",\"Digital twins + AI for predictive and prescriptive operations.\",\"Robotics and automation orchestration as a platform strategy.\",\"Operational KPIs: throughput, quality, OEE, capacity unlock, and downtime reduction.\",\"Risk management: cybersecurity, governance, and safe autonomy.\",\"Workforce enablement: upskilling, human-in-the-loop operations, and change management.\"]}\nCitations:\n[{\"apa\":\"Gaus, T., & Schlotterbeck, M. (2025, May 1). 2025 Smart Manufacturing and Operations Survey: Navigating challenges to implementation. Deloitte Insights.\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.deloitte.com\\/us\\/en\\/insights\\/industry\\/manufacturing\\/2025-smart-manufacturing-survey.html\",\"relevance\":\"Provides manufacturing-specific survey data on perceived competitiveness drivers and reported improvements (e.g., output, productivity, and capacity), plus common implementation challenges such as talent and operational risk.\"},{\"apa\":\"Singla, A., Sukharevsky, A., Hall, B., Yee, L., & Chui, M. (2025, November 5). The state of AI in 2025: Agents, innovation, and transformation. McKinsey & Company.\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.mckinsey.com\\/capabilities\\/quantumblack\\/our-insights\\/the-state-of-ai\",\"relevance\":\"Documents that AI use is widespread but scaling remains limited, and highlights workflow redesign as a key success factor. Useful to frame why manufacturers must move beyond pilots to capture enterprise-level value.\"},{\"apa\":\"Deloitte. (2026). The State of AI in the Enterprise: Deloitte\\u2019s 2026 AI report tracking adoption and impact. Deloitte AI Institute.\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.deloitte.com\\/us\\/en\\/what-we-do\\/capabilities\\/applied-artificial-intelligence\\/content\\/state-of-ai-in-the-enterprise.html\",\"relevance\":\"Adds enterprise AI adoption context, including access expansion, governance gaps for agentic systems, and the primacy of AI fluency\\/skills development\\u2014directly supporting the article\\u2019s governance and workforce sections.\"},{\"apa\":\"Gartner. (n.d.). Smart factory trends for manufacturing industries. Gartner.\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.gartner.com\\/en\\/supply-chain\\/trends\\/smart-factory-trends\",\"relevance\":\"Defines smart factory operations as a strategic trend and frames practical questions leaders ask: measuring value, core technologies used, lessons learned, and success factors. Useful for structuring the article into decision-oriented sections.\"},{\"apa\":\"Le Clair, C., & Schaffrik, B. (2024, February 23). AI is reshaping automation markets: A guide to process tool evolution. Forrester.\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.forrester.com\\/report\\/ai-is-reshaping-automation-markets\\/RES180584\",\"relevance\":\"Supports the platformization theme: consolidation of automation tool markets and a shift toward \\u201cautomation fabric\\u201d concepts. This helps explain why orchestration and integrated process intelligence matter for manufacturing automation strategies.\"}]','{\"id\":\"chatcmpl-D3Vyq0hqKiwS2v7AxXSRXWv8p9e8I\",\"object\":\"chat.completion\",\"created\":1769730288,\"model\":\"gpt-4.1-2025-04-14\",\"choices\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"{\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"AI-Driven Automation in Manufacturing: How Smart Factories Will Transform 2024\\u2019s Industrial Landscape\\\",\\n  \\\"draft\\\": \\\"Overview:\\\\n\\\\nAs manufacturers confront continued supply chain volatility and demands for higher operational productivity, 2024 is shaping up as a pivotal year for AI-driven automation. Smart factories, once experimental, are maturing into networked, data-rich environments where AI, robotics, and digital twins directly lift output, quality, and resilience. This article examines how leading firms are moving from pilots to measurable impact, clarifies key enablers and challenges, and offers a blueprint for executives aiming to capitalize on this industrial revolution.\\\\n\\\\nContext: From Hype to Operational Value\\\\n\\\\nRecent survey data underscores a fast-growing consensus: smart manufacturing is now seen as essential for competitiveness, not just a future vision (Gaus & Schlotterbeck, 2025). Manufacturers are reporting hard gains\\u2014such as productivity growth, capacity unlock, and increased throughput\\u2014as digital technologies are embedded into critical workflows. However, the journey from pilot to scale is fraught with challenges: skills gaps, integration complexity, and operational risks that demand urgent attention to governance and cybersecurity.\\\\n\\\\n2024\\u2019s Distinctive Shifts\\\\n\\\\nThe year brings distinctive changes to the smart factory story:\\\\n- **Scaling Success:** Organizations are moving beyond isolated solutions by rethinking processes and embedding AI into daily operations\\u2014not simply deploying technology but redesigning how work is done (Singla et al., 2025).\\\\n- **Platformization and Orchestration:** Robotics and automation are increasingly managed via interoperable platforms, prioritized for open architecture, real-time orchestration, and robust process intelligence (Le Clair & Schaffrik, 2024).\\\\n- **Convergence of Digital Twins and AI:** Modern plants combine real-time data, asset simulation, and AI for predictive and prescriptive control of quality, maintenance, and bottleneck management, creating closed-loop operations (Gartner, n.d.).\\\\n\\\\nKey Use Cases and Repeatable Patterns\\\\n\\\\n**1. Predictive Quality and Throughput**\\\\nBy pairing AI analytics with production data, manufacturers identify root causes of defects, adjust parameters in real time, and lift first-pass yield. Examples include AI-powered vision systems on assembly lines and digital twins predicting output variability.\\\\n\\\\n**2. Dynamic Maintenance Optimization**\\\\nDigital twins of critical assets enable predictive maintenance, reducing unplanned downtime and boosting OEE (Overall Equipment Effectiveness). Workflows are redesigned to prioritize issues based on real-time risk, powered by AI monitoring.\\\\n\\\\n**3. Autonomous Robotics in Integrated Workflows**\\\\nPlug-and-play robot cells, guided by orchestration platforms and AI agent-based work allocation, automate material transport, inspection, and low-volume assembly. These systems prioritize task flexibility, exception handling, and OT system compatibility.\\\\n\\\\nEnabling Capabilities: Building the Foundation for Scale\\\\n\\\\n- **Data and Connectivity:** Unified, governed data layers underpin effective AI\\/robotics (Deloitte, 2026). Leaders invest in robust sensing, secure data integration, and standard interfaces across OT\\/IT boundaries.\\\\n- **AI and Digital Twin Maturity:** The most advanced applications feature AI-driven digital twins not just for simulation but for continuous, closed-loop optimization\\u2014allowing predictive and even autonomous process control.\\\\n- **Robotics as a Platform:** Manufacturers are shifting away from siloed robot use, adopting platforms for lifecycle management, orchestration across multiple assets, and technology-agnostic process automation.\\\\n\\\\nRisk Management: Cybersecurity, Governance, and Skills\\\\n\\\\n- **Cyber and Safety:** Expanding connectivity and autonomy expands risk; mature programs institute strict OT security protocols, continuous model monitoring, and clear governance roles.\\\\n- **Skills and Workforce:** Closing the skills gap is now a first-order priority. Organizations that proactively upskill talent\\u2014not just on AI tools, but also on new workflows and collaborative robotics\\u2014see the most sustainable results (Deloitte, 2026).\\\\n\\\\nPractical Implementation: Roadmap and Guardrails\\\\n\\\\n- **Start small but plan for scale:** Begin with high-value assets or lines, validate measurable KPI improvements, and expand via a multi-site playbook.\\\\n- **Prioritize integration and orchestration:** Select open, interoperable platforms, and design for process intelligence, not just automation.\\\\n- **Institutionalize governance and upskilling:** Define clear responsibilities for model life cycles, cyber hygiene, and continuous workforce enablement to reduce operational risk.\\\\n\\\\nConclusion:\\\\n\\\\nAI-driven smart factories are no longer aspirational\\u2014they are becoming the new standard for industrial competitiveness in 2024. By focusing on repeatable use cases, digital twin + AI convergence, integrated robotics platforms, and robust governance, manufacturers can unlock substantial gains in throughput, quality, and resilience. The future of manufacturing belongs to those who can scale these innovations safely, strategically, and across the enterprise.\\\",\\n  \\\"key_points\\\": [\\n    \\\"Manufacturers now view smart factories as key competitiveness drivers, with survey data showing measurable improvements in output, quality, and capacity.\\\",\\n    \\\"Scaling AI and automation requires not just technology, but business process redesign and workflow integration.\\\",\\n    \\\"Digital twins combined with AI are delivering predictive and prescriptive benefits in areas like maintenance, quality, and asset performance.\\\",\\n    \\\"Robotics adoption is shifting to integrated, orchestrated platforms\\u2014reducing integration and lifecycle risks.\\\",\\n    \\\"Cybersecurity, governance, and workforce upskilling are now critical constraints that determine smart manufacturing\\u2019s success.\\\",\\n    \\\"Implementation best practices: start focused, expand via repeatable playbooks, prioritize open platforms, and institutionalize governance.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"citations\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"2025 Smart Manufacturing and Operations Survey: Navigating challenges to implementation\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.deloitte.com\\/us\\/en\\/insights\\/industry\\/manufacturing\\/2025-smart-manufacturing-survey.html\\\",\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Large-scale survey evidence indicates manufacturers increasingly view smart manufacturing as a competitiveness driver over the near term. Reported impacts cluster around output, productivity, and capacity gains rather than abstract \'digital transformation\' narratives.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"The state of AI in 2025: Agents, innovation, and transformation\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.mckinsey.com\\/capabilities\\/quantumblack\\/our-insights\\/the-state-of-ai\\\",\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"AI use is widespread but scaling remains limited, and highlights workflow redesign as a key success factor. Useful to frame why manufacturers must move beyond pilots to capture enterprise-level value.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"The State of AI in the Enterprise: Deloitte\\u2019s 2026 AI report tracking adoption and impact\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.deloitte.com\\/us\\/en\\/what-we-do\\/capabilities\\/applied-artificial-intelligence\\/content\\/state-of-ai-in-the-enterprise.html\\\",\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Enterprise AI adoption context, including rapid access expansion, governance gaps for agentic systems, and the primacy of AI fluency and skills development\\u2014directly supporting the article\\u2019s governance and workforce sections.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Smart factory trends for manufacturing industries\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.gartner.com\\/en\\/supply-chain\\/trends\\/smart-factory-trends\\\",\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Defines smart factory operations as a strategic trend and frames practical questions leaders ask: measuring value, core technologies used, lessons learned, and success factors.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"AI is reshaping automation markets: A guide to process tool evolution\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.forrester.com\\/report\\/ai-is-reshaping-automation-markets\\/RES180584\\\",\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Supports the platformization theme: consolidation of automation tool markets and a shift toward \'automation fabric\' concepts. This helps explain why orchestration and integrated process intelligence matter for manufacturing automation strategies.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\",\"refusal\":null,\"annotations\":[]},\"logprobs\":null,\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}],\"usage\":{\"prompt_tokens\":1846,\"completion_tokens\":1631,\"total_tokens\":3477,\"prompt_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":1792,\"audio_tokens\":0},\"completion_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":0,\"audio_tokens\":0,\"accepted_prediction_tokens\":0,\"rejected_prediction_tokens\":0}},\"service_tier\":\"default\",\"system_fingerprint\":\"fp_1a2c4a5ede\"}',NULL,NULL,'1',1846,1631,67390,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1,'planner-author-d12abca8-83b584c8-1769730287','2026-01-29 23:44:47','2026-01-29 23:45:59'),('23a56f86-4e0b-4244-97a3-a555427049e5','a38c0b3c-9f4b-4b47-a1bc-e03e2380cd57',NULL,'gpt-5.2','completed','Act as an Editorial Planning Assistant. Create a structured framework that is ready for human consumption.\nReturn ONLY valid JSON.\nSchema:\n{\n\"framework\":{\n  \"title\":\"\",\n  \"overview\":\"\",\n  \"context\":\"\",\n  \"application\":{\"intended_reader\":\"\",\"use_case\":\"\"},\n  \"observations\":[{\"headline\":\"\",\"detail\":\"\"}],\n  \"key_themes\":[\"\"]\n},\n\"citations\":[{\"apa\":\"\",\"url\":\"\",\"relevance\":\"\"}]\n}\nTone: concise, authoritative, and practical. Use complete sentences.\nObservations: 4–6 items, each with a headline and 2–4 sentences of detail.\nCitations: 3–5 items; provide APA style in \"apa\" and a 1–2 sentence relevance note.\nArticle:\n{\"id\":\"ai-automation-smart-manufacturing-trends-2024\",\"title\":\"AI-Driven Automation in Manufacturing: How Smart Factories Will Transform 2024\\u2019s Industrial Landscape\",\"brief\":\"Explore how manufacturers are leveraging AI, robotics, and digital twins to drive efficiency, quality, and operational resilience. This article provides a data-backed look at adoption trends, real-world use cases, and the near-future of smart manufacturing in a post-pandemic economy.\",\"keywords\":[\"AI-driven automation\",\"smart manufacturing\",\"digital twins\",\"industrial robots\",\"factory efficiency\",\"manufacturing transformation\"],\"recommended_word_count\":\"1500-2500\",\"topic_coverage_level\":\"Important and Not Covered\"}\nCitations:\n[{\"title\":\"AI Is Reshaping Automation Markets | Forrester\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.forrester.com\\/report\\/ai-is-reshaping-automation-markets\\/RES180584\",\"source\":\"www.forrester.com\",\"snippet\":\"Look for the independent DPA, RPA, and process intelligence markets to merge by 2026, paving the way for comprehensive automation fabric platforms.\"},{\"title\":\"The State of AI in the Enterprise - 2026 AI report  | Deloitte US\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.deloitte.com\\/us\\/en\\/what-we-do\\/capabilities\\/applied-artificial-intelligence\\/content\\/state-of-ai-in-the-enterprise.html\",\"source\":\"www.deloitte.com\",\"snippet\":\"Explore the Deloitte AI Institute\\u2019s State of AI in the Enterprise report tracking AI investments, adoption, impacts on business, and challenges throughout 2025.\"},{\"title\":\"The State of AI: Global Survey 2025 | McKinsey\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.mckinsey.com\\/capabilities\\/quantumblack\\/our-insights\\/the-state-of-ai\",\"source\":\"www.mckinsey.com\",\"snippet\":\"\"},{\"title\":\"2025 Smart manufacturing survey | Deloitte Insights\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.deloitte.com\\/us\\/en\\/insights\\/industry\\/manufacturing\\/2025-smart-manufacturing-survey.html\",\"source\":\"www.deloitte.com\",\"snippet\":\"This study shows how smart factories boost agility, attract talent and increase productivity. Learn the challenges, technologies and practices of industry 4.0.\"},{\"title\":\"Smart Factory Trends for Smart Manufacturing\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.gartner.com\\/en\\/supply-chain\\/trends\\/smart-factory-trends\",\"source\":\"www.gartner.com\",\"snippet\":\"Smart factory operations are among top 10 smart manufacturing trends. Ensure successful digital factory operations: 4 questions about smart factories answered.\"}]','{\"id\":\"chatcmpl-D3QS0z3aIhb1aDUTp1IWCuzp6ezDA\",\"object\":\"chat.completion\",\"created\":1769709032,\"model\":\"gpt-5.2-2025-12-11\",\"choices\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"{\\n  \\\"framework\\\": {\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Editorial Framework: AI-Driven Automation in Manufacturing (Smart Factories) \\u2014 2024 Playbook\\\",\\n    \\\"overview\\\": \\\"This framework structures a 1,500\\u20132,500 word article explaining how AI, robotics, and digital twins are moving smart factories from pilots to measurable operational impact. It emphasizes what is changing in 2024: faster scaling, workflow redesign, and tighter governance, cybersecurity, and workforce enablement. The goal is to connect technology choices to concrete plant-floor outcomes (throughput, quality, uptime, and resilience).\\\",\\n    \\\"context\\\": \\\"Manufacturers are accelerating smart manufacturing programs as supply volatility and margin pressure reward higher productivity, agility, and operational transparency. Recent surveys show broad conviction that smart manufacturing will drive competitiveness, but many initiatives still face common barriers: talent gaps, complex transformations, and operational risk. Editorially, the opportunity is to translate the \\u201csmart factory\\u201d concept into an actionable roadmap with examples and metrics readers can use to benchmark progress.\\\",\\n    \\\"application\\\": {\\n      \\\"intended_reader\\\": \\\"Manufacturing executives, plant leaders, operations\\/OT leaders, and digital transformation program owners.\\\",\\n      \\\"use_case\\\": \\\"Use this framework to outline a practical, evidence-led article that prioritizes high-value use cases (quality, throughput, maintenance, and planning), clarifies enabling capabilities (data foundation, digital twins, robotics, and AI), and provides implementation guardrails (cybersecurity, governance, and workforce upskilling).\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"observations\\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\\"headline\\\": \\\"Smart manufacturing is shifting from promise to value realization.\\\",\\n        \\\"detail\\\": \\\"Large-scale survey evidence indicates manufacturers increasingly view smart manufacturing as a competitiveness driver over the near term. Reported impacts cluster around output, productivity, and capacity gains rather than abstract \\u201cdigital transformation\\u201d narratives. The article should foreground specific operational KPIs and show how they are achieved (instrumentation, analytics, and process changes), not just the technologies involved.\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"headline\\\": \\\"Scaling is still the hard part; workflow redesign is a differentiator.\\\",\\n        \\\"detail\\\": \\\"Across industries, many organizations remain stuck in experimentation or piloting, even as AI use becomes common. The strongest results correlate with redesigning workflows and embedding AI into day-to-day decision loops, not simply deploying models. Position 2024 as the year manufacturers move from isolated pilots (e.g., one line) to repeatable patterns (multi-site playbooks).\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"headline\\\": \\\"Digital twins and AI converge as the operating model for the modern plant.\\\",\\n        \\\"detail\\\": \\\"Digital twins are most compelling when paired with AI for prediction, optimization, and closed-loop control\\u2014especially in bottleneck management, quality, and asset performance. The narrative should explain how twins connect engineering, operations, and maintenance via a common data layer. Include guidance on where to start (one asset\\/line, then expand) and what \\u201cdone\\u201d looks like (validated models, governed data, and measurable KPI lift).\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"headline\\\": \\\"Robotics adoption is being reshaped by AI, autonomy, and orchestration.\\\",\\n        \\\"detail\\\": \\\"Robots are increasingly integrated into broader automation platforms where AI coordinates tasks, exceptions, and real-time work allocation. This changes vendor decisions and architecture: manufacturers must plan for interoperability, orchestration, and process intelligence rather than single-point automations. Emphasize selection criteria that reduce integration risk (open interfaces, OT compatibility, and lifecycle support).\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"headline\\\": \\\"Cybersecurity, governance, and skills are now first-order constraints.\\\",\\n        \\\"detail\\\": \\\"As plants connect more assets and deploy more autonomous capabilities, operational risk expands and requires stronger controls, oversight models, and cyber investment. Multiple reports highlight that governance maturity can lag technology adoption, especially for more autonomous systems. The article should provide a practical checklist: governance roles, model monitoring, OT security controls, and workforce upskilling plans.\\\"\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \\\"key_themes\\\": [\\n      \\\"From pilots to scale: repeatable use-case factories and multi-site rollout patterns.\\\",\\n      \\\"Digital twins + AI for predictive and prescriptive operations.\\\",\\n      \\\"Robotics and automation orchestration as a platform strategy.\\\",\\n      \\\"Operational KPIs: throughput, quality, OEE, capacity unlock, and downtime reduction.\\\",\\n      \\\"Risk management: cybersecurity, governance, and safe autonomy.\\\",\\n      \\\"Workforce enablement: upskilling, human-in-the-loop operations, and change management.\\\"\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  \\\"citations\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"apa\\\": \\\"Gaus, T., & Schlotterbeck, M. (2025, May 1). 2025 Smart Manufacturing and Operations Survey: Navigating challenges to implementation. Deloitte Insights.\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.deloitte.com\\/us\\/en\\/insights\\/industry\\/manufacturing\\/2025-smart-manufacturing-survey.html\\\",\\n      \\\"relevance\\\": \\\"Provides manufacturing-specific survey data on perceived competitiveness drivers and reported improvements (e.g., output, productivity, and capacity), plus common implementation challenges such as talent and operational risk.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"apa\\\": \\\"Singla, A., Sukharevsky, A., Hall, B., Yee, L., & Chui, M. (2025, November 5). The state of AI in 2025: Agents, innovation, and transformation. McKinsey & Company.\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.mckinsey.com\\/capabilities\\/quantumblack\\/our-insights\\/the-state-of-ai\\\",\\n      \\\"relevance\\\": \\\"Documents that AI use is widespread but scaling remains limited, and highlights workflow redesign as a key success factor. Useful to frame why manufacturers must move beyond pilots to capture enterprise-level value.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"apa\\\": \\\"Deloitte. (2026). The State of AI in the Enterprise: Deloitte\\u2019s 2026 AI report tracking adoption and impact. Deloitte AI Institute.\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.deloitte.com\\/us\\/en\\/what-we-do\\/capabilities\\/applied-artificial-intelligence\\/content\\/state-of-ai-in-the-enterprise.html\\\",\\n      \\\"relevance\\\": \\\"Adds enterprise AI adoption context, including access expansion, governance gaps for agentic systems, and the primacy of AI fluency\\/skills development\\u2014directly supporting the article\\u2019s governance and workforce sections.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"apa\\\": \\\"Gartner. (n.d.). Smart factory trends for manufacturing industries. Gartner.\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.gartner.com\\/en\\/supply-chain\\/trends\\/smart-factory-trends\\\",\\n      \\\"relevance\\\": \\\"Defines smart factory operations as a strategic trend and frames practical questions leaders ask: measuring value, core technologies used, lessons learned, and success factors. Useful for structuring the article into decision-oriented sections.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"apa\\\": \\\"Le Clair, C., & Schaffrik, B. (2024, February 23). AI is reshaping automation markets: A guide to process tool evolution. Forrester.\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.forrester.com\\/report\\/ai-is-reshaping-automation-markets\\/RES180584\\\",\\n      \\\"relevance\\\": \\\"Supports the platformization theme: consolidation of automation tool markets and a shift toward \\u201cautomation fabric\\u201d concepts. This helps explain why orchestration and integrated process intelligence matter for manufacturing automation strategies.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\",\"refusal\":null,\"annotations\":[]},\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}],\"usage\":{\"prompt_tokens\":10073,\"completion_tokens\":1534,\"total_tokens\":11607,\"prompt_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":0,\"audio_tokens\":0},\"completion_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":0,\"audio_tokens\":0,\"accepted_prediction_tokens\":0,\"rejected_prediction_tokens\":0}},\"service_tier\":\"default\",\"system_fingerprint\":null}',NULL,NULL,'1',10073,1534,394230,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1,'planner-fw-d12abca8-83b584c8-r1769709023','2026-01-29 17:50:24','2026-01-29 17:51:01'),('275b4146-dbc9-4fb4-8ce0-d209854561b2','a38c0b3c-9f4b-4b47-a1bc-e03e2380cd57',NULL,'gpt-4.1','completed','You are the Author Agent. Write a draft article based on the provided framework.\nReturn ONLY valid JSON.\nSchema: {\"title\":\"\"