 \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Customer self-service and service as a differentiator are key industry trends.\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"3 Field Service Trends Today\'s Leaders Need to Know\\\",\\n          \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.salesforce.com\\/service\\/field-service-management\\/trends\\/\\\",\\n          \\\"source\\\": \\\"Salesforce\\\",\\n          \\\"date\\\": \\\"2024\\\",\\n          \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"Customer expectations rise, as technicians face burnout in a worker shortage.\\\",\\n          \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Customer expectations rise, as technicians face burnout in a worker shortage.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \\\"recommended_word_count\\\": \\\"1500-2500\\\",\\n      \\\"topic_coverage_level\\\": \\\"Important and Not Covered\\\",\\n      \\\"audience_segment\\\": \\\"Customer Experience Executives, Service Directors\\\",\\n      \\\"priority_score\\\": 0.85,\\n      \\\"opening_hook\\\": \\\"Are your customers demanding faster, more convenient support? Explore how leading B2B field service firms are boosting loyalty and efficiency through cutting-edge self-service platforms.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"blended-workforce-2024-strategies\\\",\\n      \\\"topic\\\": \\\"Blended Workforce and Technician Shortage\\\",\\n      \\\"headline\\\": \\\"Navigating the Technician Shortage: Blended Workforce Strategies for B2B Field Service\\\",\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Analyze the shift towards blended workforces in field service, uncovering fresh strategies for mitigating technician burnout and addressing talent shortages through flexible staffing and gig-economy models.\\\",\\n      \\\"key_points\\\": [\\n        \\\"Trends in blended workforce adoption for B2B field service\\\",\\n        \\\"The impact of technician burnout on productivity and service delivery\\\",\\n        \\\"Integrating freelancers and contractors: benefits and pitfalls\\\",\\n        \\\"Technology\'s role in supporting a mobile, flexible workforce\\\",\\n        \\\"Talent acquisition tactics for a competitive service industry\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"keywords\\\": [\\n        \\\"blended workforce\\\",\\n        \\\"technician shortage\\\",\\n        \\\"burnout\\\",\\n        \\\"gig economy\\\",\\n        \\\"field service staffing\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"citations\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"2024 Voice of the Field Service Engineer: The Trend, The Surprise, and The Red Flag\\\",\\n          \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/servicecouncil.com\\/reports\\/2024-voice-of-the-field-service-engineer-the-trend-the-surprise-and-the-red-flag\\/\\\",\\n          \\\"source\\\": \\\"Service Council\\\",\\n          \\\"date\\\": \\\"Jan 10, 2025\\\",\\n          \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"Concerning insights into the state of field service work.\\\",\\n          \\\"quote\\\": \\\"The 2024 Voice of the Field Service Engineer survey uncovered some surprising \\u2013 and concerning \\u2013 insights into the state of field service work.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \\\"recommended_word_count\\\": \\\"1500-2500\\\",\\n      \\\"topic_coverage_level\\\": \\\"Important and Not Covered\\\",\\n      \\\"audience_segment\\\": \\\"HR and Workforce Management Leaders, Field Operations Executives\\\",\\n      \\\"priority_score\\\": 0.87,\\n      \\\"opening_hook\\\": \\\"Is technician burnout threatening your service levels? Uncover proven blended workforce strategies that help B2B service organizations thrive despite labor shortages.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"predictive-analytics-mobile-visibility\\\",\\n      \\\"topic\\\": \\\"Connected Data and Predictive Analytics\\\",\\n      \\\"headline\\\": \\\"Leveraging Connected Data: How Real-Time Analytics Are Transforming Field Service\\\",\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"This data-driven article explains how B2B field service teams are achieving real-time visibility with mobile platforms and predictive analytics, generating advanced insights that optimize resource allocation and service quality.\\\",\\n      \\\"key_points\\\": [\\n        \\\"Role of mobile solutions in real-time operations management\\\",\\n        \\\"Predictive analytics for maintenance scheduling and resource optimization\\\",\\n        \\\"Boosting first-time fix rates with connected data streams\\\",\\n        \\\"Challenges in integrating analytics into legacy field platforms\\\",\\n        \\\"Case studies of ROI from predictive analytics implementations\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"keywords\\\": [\\n        \\\"connected data\\\",\\n        \\\"predictive analytics\\\",\\n        \\\"mobile solutions\\\",\\n        \\\"real-time visibility\\\",\\n        \\\"field service analytics\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"citations\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"Year-end Recap: A Look Back at the 2024 Top Trends in Field Service\\\",\\n          \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.servicepower.com\\/blog\\/2024-year-end-recap\\\",\\n          \\\"source\\\": \\\"ServicePower\\\",\\n          \\\"date\\\": \\\"Dec 18, 2024\\\",\\n          \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"Analytics for field service optimization and predictive analytics are among top 2024 trends.\\\",\\n          \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Analytics for field service optimization and predictive analytics are among top 2024 trends.\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"3 Field Service Trends Today\'s Leaders Need to Know\\\",\\n          \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.salesforce.com\\/service\\/field-service-management\\/trends\\/\\\",\\n          \\\"source\\\": \\\"Salesforce\\\",\\n          \\\"date\\\": \\\"2024\\\",\\n          \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"Mobile workers thrive with connected data. AI is no longer optional.\\\",\\n          \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Mobile workers thrive with connected data. AI is no longer optional.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \\\"recommended_word_count\\\": \\\"1500-2500\\\",\\n      \\\"topic_coverage_level\\\": \\\"Important and Not Covered\\\",\\n      \\\"audience_segment\\\": \\\"Field Service IT Directors, Digital Transformation Leaders\\\",\\n      \\\"priority_score\\\": 0.89,\\n      \\\"opening_hook\\\": \\\"Are you leveraging the full power of real-time data? Explore the B2B field service analytics revolution\\u2014where predictive intelligence boosts efficiency and customer satisfaction.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\",\"refusal\":null,\"annotations\":[]},\"logprobs\":null,\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}],\"usage\":{\"prompt_tokens\":1931,\"completion_tokens\":1928,\"total_tokens\":3859,\"prompt_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":0,\"audio_tokens\":0},\"completion_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":0,\"audio_tokens\":0,\"accepted_prediction_tokens\":0,\"rejected_prediction_tokens\":0}},\"service_tier\":\"default\",\"system_fingerprint\":\"fp_1a2c4a5ede\"}',NULL,NULL,'1',1931,1928,77150,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1,'planner-synopses-86e75186-3fcc-4b5b-8bc1-4b5329ee120b-1769603164','2026-01-28 12:26:05','2026-01-28 12:26:35'),('3d0a6df2-6bcd-4932-88f0-eea87abdbfcb','a38c0b3c-9f4b-4b47-a1bc-e03e2380cd57',NULL,'gpt-4.1','completed','You are the Author Agent. Write a draft article based on the provided framework.\nReturn ONLY valid JSON.\nSchema: {\"title\":\"\",\"draft\":\"\",\"key_points\":[\"\"],\"citations\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"url\":\"\",\"quote\":\"\"}]}\nArticle headline: Digital Twins and AI: Quality Breakthroughs for Smart Manufacturers in 2024\nSynopsis: This piece dives into the integration of digital twins and AI, examining how they drive unprecedented quality control and predictive performance in modern manufacturing facilities.\nKeywords: digital twins, smart factories, AI quality control, manufacturing simulation, predictive analytics, advanced robotics\nFramework:\n{\"title\":\"Digital Twins and AI: Quality Breakthroughs for Smart Manufacturers in 2024\",\"overview\":\"This editorial framework explains how digital twins and AI combine to improve manufacturing quality outcomes through real-time monitoring, predictive analytics, and prescriptive decision support. It prioritizes practical implementation patterns, quality-centric use cases, and data\\/architecture requirements. The structure supports a 1,500\\u20132,500 word article aimed at operations leaders evaluating where to start and how to scale.\",\"context\":\"Smart manufacturing programs are moving from experimentation to measurable value, but quality remains constrained by limited visibility, siloed data, and slow root-cause resolution. Digital twins provide a continuously updated virtual representation of products, assets, and factory systems, enabling simulation and \\u201cwhat-if\\u201d analysis without disrupting production. Adding AI shifts twins from passive models toward prescriptive, self-optimizing systems that can detect anomalies, predict failures, and recommend optimal process settings when data fidelity and system alignment are strong.\",\"application\":{\"intended_reader\":\"Manufacturing executives, plant managers, quality leaders, and Industry 4.0 program owners.\",\"use_case\":\"Plan and prioritize a 2024 roadmap for deploying AI-enabled digital twins to improve quality control, reduce defects, and increase throughput with clear data, integration, and change-management requirements.\"},\"observations\":[{\"headline\":\"AI turns digital twins into prescriptive quality systems.\",\"detail\":\"Digital twins bridge physical and virtual operations to enable real-time monitoring and predictive analytics, but AI expands them into autonomous, decision-capable systems. Recent manufacturing literature describes an evolution from passive simulation to prescriptive, self-optimizing twins that can optimize scheduling, control variables, and enhance quality control. For editorial planning, emphasize that quality gains come from closed-loop learning and action, not visualization alone.\"},{\"headline\":\"Use-case clarity matters because \\u201cdigital twin\\u201d spans multiple scopes.\",\"detail\":\"Digital twins can be built at product, asset, factory, or end-to-end supply chain scope, and each scope answers different operational questions. Product twins support defect root-cause analysis and warranty analytics, while asset and factory twins enable yield\\/throughput optimization and dynamic scheduling. The article should guide readers to choose the twin scope based on the specific quality constraint (e.g., defect mechanisms vs. line bottlenecks).\"},{\"headline\":\"Value is measurable when twins integrate operational data and decision workflows.\",\"detail\":\"Factory twins can compress decision cycles by simulating \\u201cwhat-if\\u201d scenarios from real-time conditions and linking outputs to scheduling and execution. Documented examples include cost savings from schedule redesign and reinforcement learning agents trained using the twin to improve sequencing outcomes compared with manual approaches. For quality-focused narratives, translate \\u201coptimization\\u201d into concrete metrics like scrap reduction, FPY improvement, and faster containment actions.\"},{\"headline\":\"Data fidelity and alignment are the gating constraints for quality breakthroughs.\",\"detail\":\"AI-enabled digital twins depend on high-fidelity, real-time data and a tight correspondence between the physical system and its digital counterpart. Manufacturing data is often fragmented across PLCs, sensors, MES, ERP, and human inputs, creating gaps that reduce model reliability and trust. The editorial plan should include a \\u201creadiness checklist\\u201d covering instrumentation, master data, data quality, and governance before promising advanced quality automation.\"},{\"headline\":\"Smart factory adoption is rising, but organizations must manage risk and talent gaps.\",\"detail\":\"Survey research indicates broad belief that smart manufacturing is becoming central to competitiveness, with reported average improvements in output, productivity, and capacity after implementation. However, implementation barriers commonly include complex transformation management, operational risk, cybersecurity needs, and workforce upskilling requirements. The article should balance opportunity with practical execution guidance: roles, operating model, and controls needed to sustain quality improvements at scale.\"}],\"key_themes\":[\"Closed-loop quality management with AI-enabled digital twins\",\"Choosing the right twin scope: product vs. asset vs. factory vs. end-to-end\",\"Real-time data integration across PLC, IoT, MES, and ERP for quality visibility\",\"Predictive and prescriptive analytics for defect prevention and process optimization\",\"Implementation readiness: data fidelity, governance, cybersecurity, and skills\"]}\nCitations:\n[{\"apa\":\"Nguyen, P., Kim, M., Nichols, E., & Yoon, H.-S. (2025). AI-driven digital twins for manufacturing: A review across hierarchical manufacturing system levels. Sensors, 26(1), 124. https:\\/\\/doi.org\\/10.3390\\/s26010124\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\\/articles\\/PMC12787485\\/\",\"relevance\":\"Provides a current synthesis of how AI integration transforms digital twins into prescriptive systems used for predictive maintenance, process optimization, quality control, and scheduling, while emphasizing data fidelity and alignment requirements.\"},{\"apa\":\"Camarella, S., Conway, M. P., Goering, K., & Huntington, M. (2024, January 10). Digital twins: The next frontier of factory optimization. McKinsey & Company. https:\\/\\/www.mckinsey.com\\/capabilities\\/operations\\/our-insights\\/digital-twins-the-next-frontier-of-factory-optimization\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.mckinsey.com\\/capabilities\\/operations\\/our-insights\\/digital-twins-the-next-frontier-of-factory-optimization\",\"relevance\":\"Defines digital twin scopes (product, asset, factory, end-to-end) and explains how factory twins support real-time decision-making, what-if simulation, and measurable operational improvements relevant to quality and throughput.\"},{\"apa\":\"Gaus, T., & Schlotterbeck, M. (2025, May 1). 2025 Smart Manufacturing and Operations Survey: Navigating challenges to implementation. Deloitte Insights. https:\\/\\/www.deloitte.com\\/us\\/en\\/insights\\/industry\\/manufacturing\\/2025-smart-manufacturing-survey.html\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.deloitte.com\\/us\\/en\\/insights\\/industry\\/manufacturing\\/2025-smart-manufacturing-survey.html\",\"relevance\":\"Offers executive survey evidence on smart manufacturing value realization and adoption barriers, including transformation complexity, operational risk, cybersecurity investments, and workforce upskilling needs.\"},{\"apa\":\"Gartner. (n.d.). Smart factory trends for manufacturing industries. Gartner. https:\\/\\/www.gartner.com\\/en\\/supply-chain\\/trends\\/smart-factory-trends\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.gartner.com\\/en\\/supply-chain\\/trends\\/smart-factory-trends\",\"relevance\":\"Frames smart factory operations as a strategic technology trend and highlights the need to measure value, select enabling technologies, learn from implementations, and define success practices that can anchor editorial guidance.\"}]','{\"id\":\"chatcmpl-D3hBHngWZEztvaLB7zzwEHotZ6X7w\",\"object\":\"chat.completion\",\"created\":1769773343,\"model\":\"gpt-4.1-2025-04-14\",\"choices\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"{\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Digital Twins and AI: Quality Breakthroughs for Smart Manufacturers in 2024\\\",\\n  \\\"draft\\\": \\\"In 2024, manufacturing leaders are directing their attention toward two rapidly converging technologies: digital twins and artificial intelligence (AI). As the sector stands on the cusp of measurable transformation, this integration promises to redefine quality management across product lines, facilities, and entire value chains.\\\\n\\\\nOverview: Practical Quality Through Digital Twins and Artificial Intelligence\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nSmart manufacturing is moving decisively from pilot projects to scaled, repeatable value. Despite this progress, quality management often remains hamstrung by fragmented data, slow diagnostic processes, and a lack of real-time visibility. Digital twins\\u2014dynamic, high-fidelity virtual models of physical products, assets, or processes\\u2014are now bridging this gap. \\\\n\\\\nAI amplifies the power of digital twins, evolving them from static visualization tools to dynamic, prescriptive, and even autonomous systems capable of detecting anomalies, preventing defects, and recommending process improvements. This next step is neither theoretical nor distant: practical use cases and industry surveys point to a measurable leap in quality, throughput, and operational agility for those who implement with strategic intent.\\\\n\\\\nContext: Why Now, and Why Quality?\\\\n-----------------------------------\\\\nIndustry 4.0 initiatives have long promised increased efficiency and competitiveness, yet quality outcomes have proven difficult to advance at scale. Legacy systems often produce siloed data, and conventional root-cause analysis or process control fails to keep pace with increasing product complexity and customer expectations. \\\\n\\\\nDigital twins allow manufacturers to simulate and optimize processes in real time, providing an up-to-date, virtual mirror of physical systems. When infused with AI, these twins move from passive observers to active copilots\\u2014continuously scanning for adverse trends, learning from operational data, and directly supporting decisions that drive measurable improvements in scrap rates, first-pass yield, and downtime.\\\\n\\\\nKey Applications: Roadmap for AI-Enabled Digital Twins\\\\n------------------------------------------------------\\\\nFor manufacturing executives and quality leaders, the immediate question is no longer \\\\\\\"if\\\\\\\" but \\\\\\\"how\\\\\\\". The most impactful applications include:\\\\n- **Quality-centric product twins** for defect root-cause analysis and warranty cost reduction.\\\\n- **Asset and process twins** for optimizing yield, reducing bottlenecks, and enabling predictive maintenance.\\\\n- **Factory and network twins** supporting what-if scenario simulations, dynamic scheduling, and rapid containment response to quality events.\\\\n\\\\nEach digital twin scope\\u2014from individual products to factory platforms and end-to-end supply chains\\u2014drives value in different ways, making clear alignment of use cases with operational challenges essential.\\\\n\\\\nObservations and Evidence\\\\n-------------------------\\\\n1. **AI turns digital twins into prescriptive quality systems.** Recent literature demonstrates that digital twins, when layered with AI, become capable not just of simulation but of autonomous action\\u2014optimizing schedules, adjusting parameters, and recommending prescriptive changes. Quality improvements are achieved by closing the loop between anomaly detection, predictive analytics, and real-time process control, not merely by improving visibility or reporting. ([Nguyen et al., 2025](https:\\/\\/pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\\/articles\\/PMC12787485\\/))\\\\n\\\\n2. **Use-case clarity is critical.** Digital twins exist on multiple scales. Choosing the right scope\\u2014product, asset, factory, or supply chain\\u2014is crucial for targeting quality pain points correctly. Product twins are invaluable for analyzing defect mechanisms, while factory twins unlock process optimization and rapid containment. ([Camarella et al., 2024](https:\\/\\/www.mckinsey.com\\/capabilities\\/operations\\/our-insights\\/digital-twins-the-next-frontier-of-factory-optimization))\\\\n\\\\n3. **Value is grounded in data and workflow integration.** Digital twins deliver tangible quality gains when they are tightly integrated with real-time operational data (from PLCs, IoT sensors, MES, ERP, and more) and link outputs directly to scheduling and process execution. Use cases include adaptive scheduling and reinforcement learning agents augmenting decision cycles. Key metrics include scrap reduction, first-pass yield (FPY) improvement, and time-to-containment. ([Camarella et al., 2024](https:\\/\\/www.mckinsey.com\\/capabilities\\/operations\\/our-insights\\/digital-twins-the-next-frontier-of-factory-optimization))\\\\n\\\\n4. **Data fidelity and system alignment are gating factors.** Advanced quality automation hinges on high-quality, real-time data and accurate mapping between the virtual and physical. Organizations must assess instrumentation, data integrity, master data management, and governance before deploying prescriptive automation. ([Nguyen et al., 2025](https:\\/\\/pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\\/articles\\/PMC12787485\\/))\\\\n\\\\n5. **Smart factory adoption is rising, but execution risks remain.** Survey data underscores that smart manufacturing is yielding concrete improvements in output and productivity, yet challenges include transformation management, cybersecurity, and workforce readiness. Successful organizations define roles, invest in upskilling, and implement controls to sustain quality breakthroughs at scale. ([Gaus & Schlotterbeck, 2025](https:\\/\\/www.deloitte.com\\/us\\/en\\/insights\\/industry\\/manufacturing\\/2025-smart-manufacturing-survey.html); [Gartner, n.d.](https:\\/\\/www.gartner.com\\/en\\/supply-chain\\/trends\\/smart-factory-trends))\\\\n\\\\nPractical Guidance: Getting Ready for Digital Twin-Driven Quality\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nManufacturers should start with a readiness checklist that covers:\\\\n- Comprehensive instrumentation and data collection\\\\n- Data governance and master data management\\\\n- Secure, scalable integration across legacy and modern platforms\\\\n- Workforce training and cross-functional collaboration\\\\n- Change management and risk mitigation planning\\\\n\\\\nConclusion: Smart manufacturers who carefully align digital twin initiatives with targeted quality objectives\\u2014while investing in data integrity and organizational readiness\\u2014are primed to achieve unprecedented gains in defect prevention, process stability, and customer satisfaction in 2024 and beyond.\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"key_points\\\": [\\n    \\\"AI-enabled digital twins advance quality control from passive monitoring to prescriptive, self-optimizing systems.\\\",\\n    \\\"Selecting the right digital twin scope is critical\\u2014product, asset, factory, or supply chain twins address different quality challenges.\\\",\\n    \\\"Real-time integration of operational data (PLC, IoT, MES, ERP) is essential for predictive analytics and closed-loop quality improvements.\\\",\\n    \\\"Data fidelity, system alignment, and governance are foundational for reliable prescriptive automation.\\\",\\n    \\\"Smart factory adoption is rising, but successful scale-up depends on managing workforce, cybersecurity, and change-management risks.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"citations\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"AI-driven digital twins for manufacturing: A review across hierarchical manufacturing system levels\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\\/articles\\/PMC12787485\\/\\\",\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"An evolution is occurring from passive digital twin simulation towards prescriptive, self-optimizing twins integrating AI to support predictive maintenance, process optimization, and direct quality control\\u2014so long as high data fidelity and alignment are present.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Digital twins: The next frontier of factory optimization\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.mckinsey.com\\/capabilities\\/operations\\/our-insights\\/digital-twins-the-next-frontier-of-factory-optimization\\\",\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Digital twins span multiple operational scopes\\u2014product, asset, factory, end-to-end\\u2014and drive measurable improvements in quality, throughput, and adaptability when tightly integrated with real-time operational data and scheduling workflows.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"2025 Smart Manufacturing and Operations Survey: Navigating challenges to implementation\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.deloitte.com\\/us\\/en\\/insights\\/industry\\/manufacturing\\/2025-smart-manufacturing-survey.html\\\",\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Surveyed executives report significant gains from smart manufacturing, but note that transformation complexity, operational risk, and workforce skills are the leading barriers to broader adoption and scale.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Smart factory trends for manufacturing industries\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.gartner.com\\/en\\/supply-chain\\/trends\\/smart-factory-trends\\\",\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"As smart factory operations advance, leaders must focus on value measurement, technology enablement, and success practices\\u2014digital twins and AI play a key enabling role when aligned with process objectives and execution readiness.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\",\"refusal\":null,\"annotations\":[]},\"logprobs\":null,\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}],\"usage\":{\"prompt_tokens\":1778,\"completion_tokens\":1741,\"total_tokens\":3519,\"prompt_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":0,\"audio_tokens\":0},\"completion_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":0,\"audio_tokens\":0,\"accepted_prediction_tokens\":0,\"rejected_prediction_tokens\":0}},\"service_tier\":\"default\",\"system_fingerprint\":\"fp_6deacce395\"}',NULL,NULL,'1',1778,1741,70009,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1,'planner-author-d12abca8-a6bba61e-1769773332','2026-01-30 11:42:13','2026-01-30 11:42:53'),('3fcd60eb-c52c-4522-9783-926528911a18','a38c0b3c-9f4b-4b47-a1bc-e03e2380cd57',NULL,'gpt-4o-mini','completed','Act as a Research & Insights Lead conducting Phase 1 (Discovery) of a content-aligned B2B research work