 digital evolution\\\",\\n          \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.productsup.com\\/blog\\/manufacturing-trends-in-2024\\/\\\",\\n          \\\"source\\\": \\\"ProductSup\\\",\\n          \\\"date\\\": \\\"Jan 17, 2024\\\",\\n          \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"Manufacturing trends emerging in 2024 include digital twins and smart manufacturing.\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"Insights for the Industrial Manufacturing Industry\\\",\\n          \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/kpmg.com\\/us\\/en\\/insights-by-industry\\/insights-industrial-manufacturing.html\\\",\\n          \\\"source\\\": \\\"KPMG\\\",\\n          \\\"date\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n          \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"Generative AI is reshaping manufacturing\\u2014reducing downtime, improving product quality.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Sustainability and Circular Economy\\\",\\n      \\\"insight_points\\\": [\\n        \\\"Growing pressure on manufacturers to adopt sustainable practices and reduce their carbon footprint.\\\",\\n        \\\"Investment in renewable energy and sustainable materials is becoming a priority.\\\",\\n        \\\"Circular economy strategies are being implemented to minimize waste and promote recycling.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"why_it_matters\\\": \\\"Sustainability is critical for compliance with regulations and meeting consumer demand for eco-friendly products, directly impacting brand reputation and market share.\\\",\\n      \\\"editorial_angles\\\": [\\n        \\\"Understanding the transition to a circular economy within manufacturing.\\\",\\n        \\\"How sustainable practices can enhance profitability and operational efficiency.\\\",\\n        \\\"Challenges in implementing sustainability programs in traditional manufacturing frameworks.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"citations\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"2024 manufacturing industry outlook\\\",\\n          \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.deloitte.com\\/us\\/en\\/insights\\/industry\\/manufacturing-industrial-products\\/manufacturing-industry-outlook\\/2024.html\\\",\\n          \\\"source\\\": \\\"Deloitte\\\",\\n          \\\"date\\\": \\\"Oct 30, 2023\\\",\\n          \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"Manufacturers face economic uncertainty and increased focus on sustainability.\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"Top 5 Industrial Manufacturing Trends in 2024\\\",\\n          \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/career.auburn.edu\\/blog\\/2024\\/11\\/06\\/top-5-industrial-manufacturing-trends-in-2024\\/\\\",\\n          \\\"source\\\": \\\"Auburn Career\\\",\\n          \\\"date\\\": \\\"Nov 6, 2024\\\",\\n          \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"Investing in sustainability is a top trend defining the manufacturing industry.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Labor Market Dynamics and Skills Gap\\\",\\n      \\\"insight_points\\\": [\\n        \\\"The manufacturing sector is experiencing a significant shortage of skilled labor, exacerbated by an aging workforce.\\\",\\n        \\\"Upskilling and reskilling programs are critical to address the skills gap and prepare for technological advancements.\\\",\\n        \\\"Attracting a younger workforce requires new incentives and engagement strategies.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"why_it_matters\\\": \\\"A skilled workforce is essential for operational efficiency and innovation. Addressing labor shortages will determine the competitiveness of the manufacturing sector.\\\",\\n      \\\"editorial_angles\\\": [\\n        \\\"Strategies for attracting and retaining talent in manufacturing.\\\",\\n        \\\"Case studies on successful upskilling initiatives.\\\",\\n        \\\"The role of educational institutions in bridging the manufacturing skills gap.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"citations\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"5 trends that will change the manufacturing industry in 2024\\\",\\n          \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.genpact.com\\/insight\\/manufacturing-in-2024-and-beyond-experience-at-the-heart-of-change\\\",\\n          \\\"source\\\": \\\"Genpact\\\",\\n          \\\"date\\\": \\\"Dec 21, 2023\\\",\\n          \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"Role-based upskilling programs fight skills gaps and workforce challenges in manufacturing.\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"2026 Manufacturing Industry Predictions\\\",\\n          \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.bdo.com\\/insights\\/industries\\/manufacturing\\/2026-manufacturing-industry-predictions\\\",\\n          \\\"source\\\": \\\"BDO\\\",\\n          \\\"date\\\": \\\"Jan 9, 2026\\\",\\n          \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"Labor market challenges will intensify in 2026 as manufacturers struggle to attract workers.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"E-Commerce and Digital Strategies\\\",\\n      \\\"insight_points\\\": [\\n        \\\"B2B E-Commerce platforms are reshaping how manufacturers engage with customers and manage sales.\\\",\\n        \\\"Integration of CRM and ERP systems with e-commerce platforms streamline operations and improve customer service.\\\",\\n        \\\"Digital marketing strategies are essential for driving online sales and enhancing brand visibility.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"why_it_matters\\\": \\\"E-commerce capabilities are crucial for manufacturers to reach new markets, improve customer interactions, and enhance operational efficiencies.\\\",\\n      \\\"editorial_angles\\\": [\\n        \\\"Best practices for integrating e-commerce in manufacturing operations.\\\",\\n        \\\"The future of B2B E-Commerce in the manufacturing sector.\\\",\\n        \\\"How to leverage digital marketing to drive e-commerce growth.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"citations\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"Manufacturing Trends 2024 \\u2013 A Year in Review\\\",\\n          \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/incit.org\\/en_us\\/thought-leadership\\/a-year-in-review-what-trends-defined-the-manufacturing-sector-in-2024\\/\\\",\\n          \\\"source\\\": \\\"INCIT\\\",\\n          \\\"date\\\": \\\"Dec 16, 2024\\\",\\n          \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"Learn about manufacturing trends including generative AI adoption and the need for e-commerce optimization.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"trend_summary\\\": [\\n    {\\\"trend\\\": \\\"Digital Transformation in Manufacturing\\\", \\\"repeated_in_research\\\": \\\"yes\\\"},\\n    {\\\"trend\\\": \\\"Sustainability and Circular Economy\\\", \\\"repeated_in_research\\\": \\\"yes\\\"},\\n    {\\\"trend\\\": \\\"Labor Market Dynamics and Skills Gap\\\", \\\"repeated_in_research\\\": \\\"yes\\\"},\\n    {\\\"trend\\\": \\\"E-Commerce and Digital Strategies\\\", \\\"repeated_in_research\\\": \\\"yes\\\"}\\n  ],\\n  \\\"candidate_keywords\\\": [],\\n  \\\"next_step_question\\\": \\\"Proceed to Research Phase 2?\\\"\\n}\\n```\",\"refusal\":null,\"annotations\":[]},\"logprobs\":null,\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}],\"usage\":{\"prompt_tokens\":2588,\"completion_tokens\":1468,\"total_tokens\":4056,\"prompt_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":0,\"audio_tokens\":0},\"completion_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":0,\"audio_tokens\":0,\"accepted_prediction_tokens\":0,\"rejected_prediction_tokens\":0}},\"service_tier\":\"default\",\"system_fingerprint\":\"fp_8bbc38b4db\"}',NULL,NULL,'1',2588,1468,1269,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1,'planner-phase1-a38c0b3c-9f4b-4b47-a1bc-e03e2380cd57','2026-01-28 14:34:24','2026-01-28 14:34:55'),('52a37a04-fb7b-4356-89ff-9ff9c9c402f5','a38c0b3c-9f4b-4b47-a1bc-e03e2380cd57',NULL,'gpt-4.1','completed','You are the Author Agent. Write a draft article based on the provided framework.\nReturn ONLY valid JSON.\nSchema: {\"title\":\"\",\"draft\":\"\",\"key_points\":[\"\"],\"citations\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"url\":\"\",\"quote\":\"\"}]}\nArticle headline: AI-Driven Automation in Manufacturing: How Smart Factories Will Transform 2024’s Industrial Landscape\nSynopsis: Explore how manufacturers are leveraging AI, robotics, and digital twins to drive efficiency, quality, and operational resilience. This article provides a data-backed look at adoption trends, real-world use cases, and the near-future of smart manufacturing in a post-pandemic economy.\nKeywords: AI-driven automation, smart manufacturing, digital twins, industrial robots, factory efficiency, manufacturing transformation\nFramework:\n{\"title\":\"Editorial Framework: AI-Driven Automation in Manufacturing (Smart Factories) \\u2014 2024 Playbook\",\"overview\":\"This framework structures a 1,500\\u20132,500 word article explaining how AI, robotics, and digital twins are moving smart factories from pilots to measurable operational impact. It emphasizes what is changing in 2024: faster scaling, workflow redesign, and tighter governance, cybersecurity, and workforce enablement. The goal is to connect technology choices to concrete plant-floor outcomes (throughput, quality, uptime, and resilience).\",\"context\":\"Manufacturers are accelerating smart manufacturing programs as supply volatility and margin pressure reward higher productivity, agility, and operational transparency. Recent surveys show broad conviction that smart manufacturing will drive competitiveness, but many initiatives still face common barriers: talent gaps, complex transformations, and operational risk. Editorially, the opportunity is to translate the \\u201csmart factory\\u201d concept into an actionable roadmap with examples and metrics readers can use to benchmark progress.\",\"application\":{\"intended_reader\":\"Manufacturing executives, plant leaders, operations\\/OT leaders, and digital transformation program owners.\",\"use_case\":\"Use this framework to outline a practical, evidence-led article that prioritizes high-value use cases (quality, throughput, maintenance, and planning), clarifies enabling capabilities (data foundation, digital twins, robotics, and AI), and provides implementation guardrails (cybersecurity, governance, and workforce upskilling).\"},\"observations\":[{\"headline\":\"Smart manufacturing is shifting from promise to value realization.\",\"detail\":\"Large-scale survey evidence indicates manufacturers increasingly view smart manufacturing as a competitiveness driver over the near term. Reported impacts cluster around output, productivity, and capacity gains rather than abstract \\u201cdigital transformation\\u201d narratives. The article should foreground specific operational KPIs and show how they are achieved (instrumentation, analytics, and process changes), not just the technologies involved.\"},{\"headline\":\"Scaling is still the hard part; workflow redesign is a differentiator.\",\"detail\":\"Across industries, many organizations remain stuck in experimentation or piloting, even as AI use becomes common. The strongest results correlate with redesigning workflows and embedding AI into day-to-day decision loops, not simply deploying models. Position 2024 as the year manufacturers move from isolated pilots (e.g., one line) to repeatable patterns (multi-site playbooks).\"},{\"headline\":\"Digital twins and AI converge as the operating model for the modern plant.\",\"detail\":\"Digital twins are most compelling when paired with AI for prediction, optimization, and closed-loop control\\u2014especially in bottleneck management, quality, and asset performance. The narrative should explain how twins connect engineering, operations, and maintenance via a common data layer. Include guidance on where to start (one asset\\/line, then expand) and what \\u201cdone\\u201d looks like (validated models, governed data, and measurable KPI lift).\"},{\"headline\":\"Robotics adoption is being reshaped by AI, autonomy, and orchestration.\",\"detail\":\"Robots are increasingly integrated into broader automation platforms where AI coordinates tasks, exceptions, and real-time work allocation. This changes vendor decisions and architecture: manufacturers must plan for interoperability, orchestration, and process intelligence rather than single-point automations. Emphasize selection criteria that reduce integration risk (open interfaces, OT compatibility, and lifecycle support).\"},{\"headline\":\"Cybersecurity, governance, and skills are now first-order constraints.\",\"detail\":\"As plants connect more assets and deploy more autonomous capabilities, operational risk expands and requires stronger controls, oversight models, and cyber investment. Multiple reports highlight that governance maturity can lag technology adoption, especially for more autonomous systems. The article should provide a practical checklist: governance roles, model monitoring, OT security controls, and workforce upskilling plans.\"}],\"key_themes\":[\"From pilots to scale: repeatable use-case factories and multi-site rollout patterns.\",\"Digital twins + AI for predictive and prescriptive operations.\",\"Robotics and automation orchestration as a platform strategy.\",\"Operational KPIs: throughput, quality, OEE, capacity unlock, and downtime reduction.\",\"Risk management: cybersecurity, governance, and safe autonomy.\",\"Workforce enablement: upskilling, human-in-the-loop operations, and change management.\"]}\nCitations:\n[{\"apa\":\"Gaus, T., & Schlotterbeck, M. (2025, May 1). 2025 Smart Manufacturing and Operations Survey: Navigating challenges to implementation. Deloitte Insights.\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.deloitte.com\\/us\\/en\\/insights\\/industry\\/manufacturing\\/2025-smart-manufacturing-survey.html\",\"relevance\":\"Provides manufacturing-specific survey data on perceived competitiveness drivers and reported improvements (e.g., output, productivity, and capacity), plus common implementation challenges such as talent and operational risk.\"},{\"apa\":\"Singla, A., Sukharevsky, A., Hall, B., Yee, L., & Chui, M. (2025, November 5). The state of AI in 2025: Agents, innovation, and transformation. McKinsey & Company.\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.mckinsey.com\\/capabilities\\/quantumblack\\/our-insights\\/the-state-of-ai\",\"relevance\":\"Documents that AI use is widespread but scaling remains limited, and highlights workflow redesign as a key success factor. Useful to frame why manufacturers must move beyond pilots to capture enterprise-level value.\"},{\"apa\":\"Deloitte. (2026). The State of AI in the Enterprise: Deloitte\\u2019s 2026 AI report tracking adoption and impact. Deloitte AI Institute.\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.deloitte.com\\/us\\/en\\/what-we-do\\/capabilities\\/applied-artificial-intelligence\\/content\\/state-of-ai-in-the-enterprise.html\",\"relevance\":\"Adds enterprise AI adoption context, including access expansion, governance gaps for agentic systems, and the primacy of AI fluency\\/skills development\\u2014directly supporting the article\\u2019s governance and workforce sections.\"},{\"apa\":\"Gartner. (n.d.). Smart factory trends for manufacturing industries. Gartner.\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.gartner.com\\/en\\/supply-chain\\/trends\\/smart-factory-trends\",\"relevance\":\"Defines smart factory operations as a strategic trend and frames practical questions leaders ask: measuring value, core technologies used, lessons learned, and success factors. Useful for structuring the article into decision-oriented sections.\"},{\"apa\":\"Le Clair, C., & Schaffrik, B. (2024, February 23). AI is reshaping automation markets: A guide to process tool evolution. Forrester.\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.forrester.com\\/report\\/ai-is-reshaping-automation-markets\\/RES180584\",\"relevance\":\"Supports the platformization theme: consolidation of automation tool markets and a shift toward \\u201cautomation fabric\\u201d concepts. This helps explain why orchestration and integrated process intelligence matter for manufacturing automation strategies.\"}]','{\"id\":\"chatcmpl-D3WR6n3TJZIsGpVqU5qtdSoeqrUfM\",\"object\":\"chat.completion\",\"created\":1769732040,\"model\":\"gpt-4.1-2025-04-14\",\"choices\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"{\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"AI-Driven Automation in Manufacturing: How Smart Factories Will Transform 2024\\u2019s Industrial Landscape\\\",\\n  \\\"draft\\\": \\\"The manufacturing sector stands at a pivotal point in 2024, as advances in artificial intelligence (AI), robotics, and digital twins turn the vision of \\\\\\\"smart factories\\\\\\\" into operational reality. With inflationary pressures, ongoing supply volatility, and heightened customer expectations reshaping the global market, manufacturers are accelerating the adoption of smart manufacturing programs, seeking measurable improvements in productivity, agility, and resilience.\\\\n\\\\n## The Case for AI-Driven Smart Factories: From Promise to Performance\\\\n\\\\nRecent industry surveys indicate a seismic shift: 86% of manufacturing leaders now believe smart manufacturing is a near-term driver of competitiveness, citing direct improvements in throughput, quality, and capacity as top outcomes. Far from just buzzwords, terms like AI-driven automation and digital twins are being directly tied to plant-floor KPIs that matter most: output, uptime, and cost-to-serve. A 2025 Deloitte survey found the greatest gains going to organizations that embedded analytics and process automation deeply into their operations, rather than keeping initiatives siloed or at the pilot stage [(Gaus & Schlotterbeck, 2025)](https:\\/\\/www.deloitte.com\\/us\\/en\\/insights\\/industry\\/manufacturing\\/2025-smart-manufacturing-survey.html).\\\\n\\\\n## The Barriers: Scaling, Talent, and Operational Risk\\\\n\\\\nYet, progress is uneven. While most manufacturers have piloted AI or automation projects, only a minority are scaling these breakthroughs across multiple sites or business units. The leading barrier? Stalled workflow redesign. Successful cases reimagine not just the tools, but the underlying decision-making loops, empowering human operators and digital systems to work as one. \\\\\\\"Scaling is still the hard part,\\\\\\\" concludes a 2025 McKinsey report, emphasizing that moving beyond pilots requires new playbooks for workflow integration, governance, and workforce enablement [(Singla et al., 2025)](https:\\/\\/www.mckinsey.com\\/capabilities\\/quantumblack\\/our-insights\\/the-state-of-ai).\\\\n\\\\n## Digital Twins Meet Closed-Loop AI\\\\n\\\\nOne of the biggest breakthroughs in 2024 is the growing convergence of digital twins and AI. Plant operators are building virtual replicas of high-value assets, lines, or entire facilities\\u2014enabling predictive maintenance, real-time performance optimization, and scenario testing. The most successful implementations pair governed data models with AI-driven analytics, allowing organizations to unlock new performance levels through simulation and closed-loop feedback. Crucially, pilot projects start small\\u2014a single compressor or bottleneck line\\u2014but rapidly expand as validated use cases demonstrate uptime improvements and waste reduction.\\\\n\\\\n## Robotics and Automation Platforms: Beyond Single-Point Solutions\\\\n\\\\nRobotics, historically an area of targeted automation, is now being re-imagined as part of an integrated automation platform. Modern systems combine industrial robots, sensors, and AI-based orchestration to assign, monitor, and optimize tasks in real time. The Forrester report on automation market evolution notes a shift to \\\\\\\"automation fabric,\\\\\\\" where interoperability and orchestration are fundamental. Manufacturers now prioritize vendors who offer open interfaces, robust OT (operational technology) compatibility, and lifecycle support, ensuring reduced integration risk and futureproof scaling [(Le Clair & Schaffrik, 2024)](https:\\/\\/www.forrester.com\\/report\\/ai-is-reshaping-automation-markets\\/RES180584).\\\\n\\\\n## Securing the Smart Factory: Governance, Cybersecurity, and Workforce Resilience\\\\n\\\\nAs factory floors grow more connected and autonomous, security and oversight concerns mount. 74% of executives in a recent Deloitte AI Institute study point to governance maturity as their top challenge for scaling enterprise AI [(Deloitte, 2026)](https:\\/\\/www.deloitte.com\\/us\\/en\\/what-we-do\\/capabilities\\/applied-artificial-intelligence\\/content\\/state-of-ai-in-the-enterprise.html). Effective programs implement robust governance roles, continuous model monitoring, OT-focused cybersecurity protocols, and workforce upskilling to reinforce AI fluency and safety. The playbook is clear: combine technology adoption with rigorous risk management and targeted training for both leadership and frontline operators.\\\\n\\\\n## What 2024 Makes Different: A Playbook for Transformation\\\\n\\\\nGartner outlines a series of strategic questions for smart factory leaders: How do you measure value? Which technologies deliver proven results? What do success stories have in common? Data shows the industry is moving from narrow pilots to multi-site, use-case-driven transformations, with a strong focus on plant-wide operational KPIs (throughput, OEE, defect reduction, and downtime minimization) [(Gartner, n.d.)](https:\\/\\/www.gartner.com\\/en\\/supply-chain\\/trends\\/smart-factory-trends).\\\\n\\\\nTo succeed, manufacturers in 2024 must embrace: \\\\n- Repeatable, high-value use cases (predictive quality, asset optimization, dynamic scheduling).\\\\n- A platform approach to data, digital twins, and robotics integration.\\\\n- Proactive governance and cybersecurity, not just technology buy-in.\\\\n- Workforce enablement, ensuring humans are empowered partners in digital transformation.\\\\n\\\\nAI-driven automation will not replace the manufacturing workforce\\u2014it will amplify it, providing the intelligence, transparency, and agility to thrive in an unpredictable world. Smart factories are no longer a distant vision but a rapidly unfolding reality\\u2014provided manufacturers focus on evidence-backed strategies, cross-functional collaboration, and the relentless pursuit of operational excellence.\\\",\\n  \\\"key_points\\\": [\\n    \\\"Smart factories in 2024 are being driven by rapid advances in AI, robotics, and digital twins, moving from pilots to full operational impact.\\\",\\n    \\\"Surveys show most manufacturers link smart manufacturing to competitiveness, but only those who redesign workflows\\u2014embedding analytics and automation\\u2014see enterprise-level gains.\\\",\\n    \\\"Digital twins, combined with AI, are now powering predictive maintenance, performance optimization, and closed-loop control, starting with small pilots and scaling as benefits become measurable.\\\",\\n    \\\"Robotics adoption is migrating toward interoperable, AI-orchestrated platforms that prioritize integration, lifecycle support, and process intelligence.\\\",\\n    \\\"Cybersecurity, governance, and workforce upskilling are first-order priorities as operational risk expands with greater connectivity and autonomy.\\\",\\n    \\\"Industry leaders are adopting repeatable use-case playbooks, focusing on plant-wide metrics such as throughput, OEE, capacity, and downtime reduction to measure transformation progress.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"citations\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"2025 Smart Manufacturing and Operations Survey: Navigating challenges to implementation\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.deloitte.com\\/us\\/en\\/insights\\/industry\\/manufacturing\\/2025-smart-manufacturing-survey.html\\\",\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Reported impacts cluster around output, productivity, and capacity gains rather than abstract \\u201cdigital transformation\\u201d narratives.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"The state of AI in 2025: Agents, innovation, and transformation\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.mckinsey.com\\/capabilities\\/quantumblack\\/our-insights\\/the-state-of-ai\\\",\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Scaling is still the hard part; the strongest results correlate with redesigning workflows and embedding AI into day-to-day decision loops, not simply deploying models.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"The State of AI in the Enterprise: Deloitte\\u2019s 2026 AI report tracking adoption and impact\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.deloitte.com\\/us\\/en\\/what-we-do\\/capabilities\\/applied-artificial-intelligence\\/content\\/state-of-ai-in-the-enterprise.html\\\",\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Governance maturity can lag technology adoption, especially for more autonomous systems.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Smart factory trends for manufacturing industries\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.gartner.com\\/en\\/supply-chain\\/trends\\/smart-factory-trends\\\",\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Defines smart factory operations as a strategic trend and frames practical questions leaders ask: measuring value, core technologies used, lessons learned, and success factors.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"AI is reshaping automation markets: A guide to process tool evolution\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https:\\/\\/www.forrester.com\\/report\\/ai-is-reshaping-automation-markets\\/RES180584\\\",\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Supports the platformization theme: consolidation of automation tool markets and a shift toward \'automation fabric\' concepts.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\",\"refusal\":null,\"annotations\":[]},\"logprobs\":null,\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}],\"usage\":{\"prompt_tokens\":1846,\"completion_tokens\":1729,\"total_tokens\":3575,\"prompt_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":1792,\"audio_tokens\":0},\"completion_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":0,\"audio_tokens\":0,\"accepted_prediction_tokens\":0,\"rejected_prediction_tokens\":0}},\"service_tier\":\"default\",\"system_fingerprint\":\"fp_6deacce395\"}',NULL,NULL,'1',1846,1729,70330,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1,'planner-author-d12abca8-83b584c8-1769732038','20